{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS1qQA4pmKEsDmPFdtsR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish fails because the similarity scores are Python floats, and boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats. Both tests pass now, including a new one that publishes two stories in a row. I didn't run the new test without the fix, so the claim that it catches the bug is untested.\n\n**Cause:** `publish()` stores `similar: [{slug, score}]`, and `similarity()` returns a float. The first publish works only because the library is empty, so `similar` is `[]` and no float is written. From the second publish on, `put_item` raises `TypeError: Float types are not supported`, and `handler()` turns that into a 500.\n\n**Fix:**\n- `src/app.py` has a new `to_dynamo()` that recursively converts floats to `Decimal`, and `publish()` now passes the item through it before `put_item`. Doing it at that point means any float added to the item later is also handled.\n- `tests/test_publish.py` has the new regression test.\n- `ANSWER.md` has the cause and the fix.\n\nOne thing I noticed but didn't change: `publish()` reads existing stories with a single `scan`, which stops at 1 MB. Once the library is large, the related list will only consider the first page of results."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1364,"cache_read_input_tokens":23593,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1364},"output_tokens":391,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d94ed7a-e3d5-46e7-9f6d-de50f9911244","uuid":"53e90925-7e82-4da0-ad37-0cae0bf75ebe","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:15:44.137Z","request_id":"req_011CgS1qPvvXzc6QadtteyeE"}
